## 6. PROGRESS LOG (newest at top — update every session)
- **[Day 2 — 2026-09-07] ✅ COMPLETE** — AI PPE detection working end-to-end:
  - Verified base YOLO (yolov8n.pt) downloads & runs (knows "person", not PPE).
  - Downloaded PPE models from Hugging Face. Tested TWO on real photos:
    * keremberke/yolov8m-hard-hat-detection → classes Hardhat / NO-Hardhat. WORKS WELL.
    * keremberke/yolov8m-protective-equipment-detection (10 classes) → detected
      almost nothing on real photos. DELETED. Lesson: more classes != better.
  - CHOSE the hard-hat model (models/ppe_model.pt). User confirmed helmet-only scope;
    vest/other PPE listed as future work.
  - Wrote app/detector.py — loads model once (cached), detect_ppe(image) returns
    annotated PIL image + summary dict (total, helmet_ok, violations, compliance %).
    Green box = helmet OK, red box = NO helmet.
  - Tuned confidence threshold: tested 0.25-0.55 on real construction photos.
    0.35 is the sweet spot (lower over-detects, higher misses real helmets). SET to 0.35.
  - Lesson learned: one stock "worker" download was an office desk → model false-
    flagged a hand/calculator as NO-Helmet. Fix = use real construction photos +
    0.35 threshold. Good story for the report (garbage-in-garbage-out, thresholds).
  - Wired detection into app/main.py Safety Detection page: upload photo → shows
    original + annotated side by side, metrics (workers/helmets/violations),
    compliance % bar, and red ALERT or green OK message.
  - 4 sample construction images kept in sample_images/. App restarts clean (HTTP 200).
  - NOTE: use st.image(..., use_container_width=True) (not deprecated use_column_width).


